    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "Door at [-1433.58, -13.73, -904.22]: BJX fork Battles.lua:16 (Npcs.json Id 46195, sh_corral_gate_01.adr). (R) the fork's own placement, not a captured one. Region The Wilds, place The Wilds."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reference",
      "evidence": "BJX fork Resources/Battles.json Id 36 ('Danger Peaks (the live dungeon: Shadow Talon ninjas and their trained eagles from the south camp round the pea'): scene sg_cliffs_of_insanity, entry, exit, 6 waves, 18 spawns ({'Shadow Talon Ninja': 5, 'Shadow Talon Blade': 6, 'Trained Eagle': 6, 'Shadow Talon Master': 1})."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Every spot inside the scene is the fork's generated layout, not an original one. Zone number 1235 is the fork's; ours must be assigned and the scene sg_cliffs_of_insanity has not been loaded by our server yet (the eleven shipped battles all use sg_random_encounter_clearing). Triggers: at-start spawns are actors, later waves follow the one before (the fork's 1.5 s delay is dropped). Knockouts and score are the design's defaults; coins and XP are the shipped battles' values, not the fork's 15 coins / 100 stars."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Not proven in the client: this scene needs one native load, and the starter or door of `entry` is drawn by the entrances work, not by this file. Each kind's rank here decides its health and hit at the fight's tier. Door actor 100000046195: reference Npcs.json Id 46195, model 15208, name 5711, at [-1433.58, -13.73, -904.22]."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) The guide's main goal is the one goal shown from the start and is done with the fork's last goal; the steps before it stay, as the triggers of its waves and boss."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reconstructed",
      "evidence": "(R) Guide overlay by scripts/dungeon_fights.py from data/content/dungeons/danger_peaks.json."
    },
    {
      "kind": "wiki",
      "evidence": "rc-0137 prize wheel: fandom 'Danger Peaks' (revision 49126) lists one prize wheel per combat job and a 70-coin slot; any other job spins the items every job's wheel holds."
